# VIGIL AI (v1.0.0) - Complete Fedora Linux Setup & Execution Guide

Everything required to install, build, run, and test Vigil AI on Fedora Linux.

---

## 1. Overview of Components

| Component | Purpose on Fedora |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Git & Core Build Tools** | Clone repository and compile native C/C++ dependencies |
| **ALSA & OpenSSL Dev Headers** | Required by the Rust native companion (`desktop/`) for microphone spectral inspection & encryption |
| **Node.js (v20 or v22 LTS) & npm** | Build the WebExtension (`dist/` & `dist-firefox/`) and execute test pipelines |
| **Rust Toolchain (rustup/cargo)** | Compile the Native Messaging companion binary (`vigil-companion`) |
| **Ollama (Linux)** | Local privacy-preserving LLM inference server (`llama3.2`, `mistral`) |
| **Web Browser** | Google Chrome, Chromium, Brave, or Mozilla Firefox |

---

## 2. Step 1: Install System Packages & C Libraries (`dnf`)

Open your terminal and install development libraries, audio packages, and Git:

```bash
# Update repositories
sudo dnf update -y

# Install build tools & development libraries
sudo dnf groupinstall -y "Development Tools"
sudo dnf install -y \
  git \
  pkgconf-pkg-config \
  openssl-devel \
  alsa-lib-devel \
  xorg-x11-server-Xvfb \
  libxcb-devel \
  libX11-devel
```

*Note: `alsa-lib-devel` is required so Rust's `cpal` crate can compile Linux audio capture for ultrasonic/voice anomaly scanning. `openssl-devel` is required for secure companion IPC.*

---

## 3. Step 2: Install Node.js (v20 or v22 LTS)

Install Node.js 22 LTS and npm directly via Fedora:

```bash
sudo dnf install -y nodejs npm

# Verify versions
node -v   # Should be v20.x or v22.x
npm -v    # Should be v10.x or newer
```

*(Alternatively with NVM: `curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.39.7/install.sh | bash && source ~/.bashrc && nvm install 22 && nvm use 22`)*

---

## 4. Step 3: Install Rust Toolchain

The native companion requires Rust and Cargo:

```bash
# Install rustup
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh -s -- -y

# Configure shell environment
source "$HOME/.cargo/env"

# Verify Rust
cargo --version
rustc --version
```

---

## 5. Step 4: Install Local AI Engine (Ollama)

Vigil AI connects locally to `http://localhost:11434`:

```bash
# Install Ollama on Linux
curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh

# Enable and start the systemd service
sudo systemctl enable --now ollama

# Pull the recommended models used by Vigil AI
ollama pull llama3.2:latest
ollama pull llama3.2:1b
ollama pull nomic-embed-text
```

Verify Ollama is responding:
```bash
curl http://localhost:11434/api/tags
```

